{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IV:title", "parent_tag": "02IV", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "section_title", "risk_level": "R1", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Catenary schemes", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-catenary}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:3f4eb131f1cc4191b7b2b409c424cef6f1174367e23305f80281a4018f2045b4", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:57643347ae84f96ce0f48cecf4fe97f5f4fb5e4d50b62b9464f28b5a5c89b547", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IV:prose-0001", "parent_tag": "02IV", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall that a topological space <MATH_0001> is called <TEXTITOPEN_0001>catenary<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if\nfor every pair of irreducible closed subsets <MATH_0002>\nthere exist a maximal chain of irreducible closed subsets\n<MATH_0003>\nand every such chain has the same length. See\nTopology, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0002": "$T \\subset T'$", "MATH_0003": "$$\nT = T_0 \\subset T_1 \\subset \\ldots \\subset T_e = T'\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-definition-catenary}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:b334419626686ec9c346fb977acddaf735a76f5e96f3065b93053364b66bc7e7", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5919d00ab232d0ec3a6ce5f63f0b38ec5463950e72d8b1c9883731445d0b1f28", "source_math_hash": "sha256:139b7d3e854b7740bba6a311aff849e6eab61de797d1922e4bf22d05b6d61f76"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IW:statement", "parent_tag": "02IV", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "definition", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. We say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>catenary<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if the\nunderlying topological space of <MATH_0003> is catenary.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0003": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-catenary}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:c46bd36d9d55e38f813011b512a8b2727cbf7cc6a967f3a7226984c35efb8459", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d4900f269937f99460c8e7c80f9c1191b7688263edb87b266e12fdc2f4d7783c", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e23f264061bb1f0c2a3e261205fa58fd93cc50d931282c2c6393f4ff9be13593"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IV:prose-0002", "parent_tag": "02IV", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall that a ring <MATH_0001> is called <TEXTITOPEN_0001>catenary<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if\nfor any pair of prime ideals <MATH_0002>\nthere exists a maximal chain of primes\n<MATH_0003>\nand all of these have the same length. See\nAlgebra, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "MATH_0001": "$A$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathfrak p \\subset \\mathfrak q$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\mathfrak p =\n\\mathfrak p_0 \\subset \\ldots \\subset \\mathfrak p_e\n= \\mathfrak q\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-definition-catenary}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:953422febc4ba03a17203947b838469397a5db46de8dcd2a1ac836804c5ff122", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5d2031dcbd33238aa906a3aa2d31b791c39298b6ffb7db9fd59355675b72d424", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7309022d3a9f53bffb8883feb24b454115c6b962e595bf6dbadc21ab3ffe0530"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IX:statement", "parent_tag": "02IV", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is catenary,\n<STRUCT_0003> there exists an open covering of <MATH_0003> all of whose members are\ncatenary schemes,\n<STRUCT_0004> for every affine open <MATH_0004> the ring\n<MATH_0005> is catenary, and\n<STRUCT_0005> there exists an affine open covering <MATH_0006> such\nthat each <MATH_0007> is the spectrum of a catenary ring.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nMoreover, in this case any locally closed subscheme of <MATH_0008> is catenary\nas well.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "MATH_0004": "$\\Spec(R) = U \\subset S$", "MATH_0005": "$R$", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "MATH_0006": "$S = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0007": "$U_i$", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}", "MATH_0008": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-catenary-local}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:f64d02c52fa2da8c08e0e7156f9a8a44df5b2454a06e55f98d491870c1441617", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d65e31f1a8eb9050fcccbe1eaf84eb0ce60cfd722c3c4708e4ad676449e7aed1", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1ba4d608b6df7547949d051a9ca7d3e77d425c7cb2a4b956b274c66a9fdbd124"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IX:proof", "parent_tag": "02IV", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Combine Topology, Lemma <REF_0001>, and\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-lemma-catenary}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-catenary}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:de8962ba6604ef56ef648423b1e062babd4b39cf1dcc5d21068471ba0996df19", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6d826bde9dc64506f555c189bef207d9d140226fc5aa1c70fb1de39b75671775", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
